  "id": "nonverbal-intelligence",
  "term": "nonverbal intelligence",
  "definition": "Nonverbal intelligence is a cognitive capacity centered on solving problems through nonlinguistic reasoning and visuospatial processing rather than through language or previously learned verbal knowledge. It is distinct from verbal intelligence and appears especially important for novel problem solving, while also supporting academic performance in areas such as language-related learning.",
